DTSTAMP:20260727T041140Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53516233684881
DTSTART:20260920T211500Z
DTEND:20260920T221500Z
DESCRIPTION:Explore Monroe Paddling Trip at 5:15 p.m.\n\nRegistration requi
 red by September 17.Trip fee is $15 per person.Limited to 10 people. Restr
 icted to ages 16 and up. All participants must have at least 2 hours of pr
 ior paddling experience OR have completed one of our Beginner Kayaking wor
 kshops.Bring your own canoe/kayak\, or rent a sit-on-top kayak (weight lim
 it: 275 pounds) for an additional $20.Location: Northfork of Salt Creek (s
 outhern section)\n\nIMPORTANT: This is a ONE-WAY trip and will require a s
 hort 5-minute carpool at the beginning and end of the trip to position veh
 icles and participants in the correct locations (between the put-in and ta
 ke-out points\, it’s 2 hours by water but only 5 minutes by road).\n\nEx
 plore the quieter side of Monroe Lake during these guided paddling trips t
 hat journey through backwaters\, wetlands\, bays\, and/or slow-moving stre
 ams. Trips highlight beautiful views\, hidden wildlife\, aquatic plants\, 
 and unique land features. Find your new favorite place to kayak! 2.5 hours
  \n\n \n\nREFUND/TRANSFER/CANCELLATION POLICY\n\nRegistrations are conside
 red final and no refunds or date transfers are available\, with limited ex
 ceptions. You may transfer a registration(s) to another person(s) by conta
 cting Jill Vance at jvance@dnr.IN.gov from the same email used in your ori
 ginal registration. Provide the name(s) and email(s) of the person to whom
  you want to transfer the registration(s). Requests must be received at le
 ast 48 hours prior to the start of the workshop.In the event that the trip
  is cancelled by the instructor for weather\, low registration\, or instru
 ctor illness\, registered participants may opt to transfer their registrat
 ion to another Explore Monroe trip on a different date or receive a full r
 efund. Weather Cancellation Policy: If only light rain is anticipated\, th
 e trip will likely proceed as scheduled. However\, if there is a strong po
 ssibility (as determined by the instructor) of moderate to heavy rain\, hi
 gh winds\, or thunder/lightning\, the workshop will be cancelled for safet
 y reasons. Any decision to cancel due to anticipated weather will be made 
 at least 2 hours prior to the trip start time. In the event of a cancellat
 ion\, an email notice will be sent to all registrants.Low Registration Pol
 icy: The trip may be cancelled\, at the discretion of the instructor\, if 
 there are fewer than 3 people signed up by the registration deadline. If t
 he trip is cancelled due to low registration\, all participants will be no
 tified within 24 hours of the close of registration.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Northfork of Salt Creek\, McGowan Road (directions e
 mailed to registrants prior to trip)
SUMMARY:Explore Monroe Paddling Trip\, Northfork of Salt Creek: southern se
 ction (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/explore-monroe-paddling-trip-nort
 hfork-of-salt-creek-southern-section-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
