UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53516315272906
DTSTART:20261004T163000Z
DTEND:20261004T173000Z
DESCRIPTION:EXTENDED-LENGTH Explore Monroe Paddling Trip at 12:30 p.m.\n\nR
 egistration required by October 1.Trip fee is $40 per person.Limited to 10
  people. Restricted to ages 16 and up. All participants must be comfortabl
 e with paddling up to 12 miles in a single outing\; this trip is not open 
 to beginner-level paddlers.Bring your own canoe/kayak\, or rent a sit-on-t
 op kayak (weight limit: 275 pounds) for an additional $20.Location: Crooke
 d Creek SRA (launch site) up the Middlefork of Salt Creek\n\nExplore the q
 uieter side of Monroe Lake during these guided paddling trips that journey
  through backwaters\, wetlands\, bays\, and/or slow-moving streams. Trips 
 highlight beautiful views\, hidden wildlife\, aquatic plants\, and unique 
 land features. Find your new favorite place to kayak! 2.5 hours \n\nBACKUP
  DATE is Friday\, October 9 (same time). Please hold the backup date in yo
 ur calendar\, in case the trip must be rescheduled due to weather or instr
 uctor illness. Refunds will be offered only if the original AND backup dat
 es are both cancelled.\n\nThis EXTENDED-LENGTH trip (about 5 hours\, expec
 ted return around 5:30 p.m.) will head up the Middlefork of Salt Creek to 
 the Elkinsville area. This is a particularly scenic portion of the Salt Cr
 eek Valley with a high likelihood of encountering bald eagles\, beavers\, 
 and other wildlife. Due to the high-water levels experienced by the reserv
 oir this summer\, we may also encounter new logjams in the narrower sectio
 ns of the creek – this trip is for those with an adventurous spirit!\n \
 n\nREFUND/TRANSFER/CANCELLATION POLICY\n\nRegistrations are considered fin
 al and no refunds or date transfers are available\, with limited exception
 s. You may transfer a registration(s) to another person(s) by contacting J
 ill Vance at jvance@dnr.IN.gov from the same email used in your original r
 egistration. Provide the name(s) and email(s) of the person to whom you wa
 nt to transfer the registration(s). Requests must be received at least 48 
 hours prior to the start of the workshop.In the event that the trip is can
 celled by the instructor for weather\, low registration\, or instructor il
 lness\, registered participants may opt to transfer their registration to 
 another Explore Monroe trip on a different date or receive a full refund. 
 Weather Cancellation Policy: If only light rain is anticipated\, the trip 
 will likely proceed as scheduled. However\, if there is a strong possibili
 ty (as determined by the instructor) of moderate to heavy rain\, high wind
 s\, or thunder/lightning\, the workshop will be cancelled for safety reaso
 ns. Any decision to cancel due to anticipated weather will be made at leas
 t 2 hours prior to the trip start time. In the event of a cancellation\, a
 n email notice will be sent to all registrants.Low Registration Policy: Th
 e trip may be cancelled\, at the discretion of the instructor\, if there a
 re fewer than 3 people signed up by the registration deadline. If the trip
  is cancelled due to low registration\, all participants will be notified 
 within 24 hours of the close of registration.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Crooked Creek State Recreation Area (TC Steele / Cro
 oked Creek Road\, Nashville)
SUMMARY:EXTENDED-LENGTH Explore Monroe Paddling Trip\, Middlefork of Salt C
 reek (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/extended-length-explore-monroe-pa
 ddling-trip-middlefork-of-salt-creek-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
