DESCRIPTION:Flora Field Day at 9:00 a.m.\n\n•    Sign up for this session
  at tinyurl.com/florafielddays \n•    Registration required by October 5
 .\n•    Free\; recommended for ages 12 and up.\n•    Session location:
  Cutright SRA\n\nWant to work on your flora identification skills? Practic
 e with a naturalist! Field day emphasis is on proper use and application o
 f an ID key\, which opens the door to identifying thousands of species. Th
 e naturalist will work with each attendee based on their prior experience.
  If you’ve never worked with flower ID before\, this is a great way to l
 earn. If you have prior experience\, this is a fun way to practice your sk
 ills (and maybe add some new blooms to your life list!). 2 hours\n\nThings
  to Bring:\n•    Newcomb’s Wildflower Guide (extra copies available\, 
 if you don’t have your own)\n•    bug spray (long pants are also a goo
 d idea!)\n•    hat and sunglasses (for sun protection)\n•    water bot
 tle (pre-filled)\n•    camera (if you’re the picture-taking type)
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Cutright SRA - directions will be emailed after regi
 stration ends
